            <ArticleTitle>Colchicine metallocenyl bioconjugates showing high antiproliferative activities against cancer cell lines.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>17041-17052</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c7dt03229c</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A series of ferrocenyl and ruthenocenyl conjugates with colchicine bearing a 1,2,3-triazole moiety were synthesized and their anticancer properties were evaluated. We found that the most potent metallocenyl derivatives Rc4 and Rc5 are 6-7 times more cytotoxic toward HepG2 cells, while Fc4 and Fc5 are two times more cytotoxic toward HCT116 cells as colchicine. We also found that compounds Fc4, Fc5, Rc1 and Rc3-Rc5 are able to induce apoptosis, while compound Fc2 arrests mitosis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
